Create a reusable Urkaaaz dark button-background family that matches the
approved gold button family in size, silhouette, proportions, and state
behavior. The dark face is a semantic color variant, not a new button shape.

## References

- Attach the approved gold backgrounds
  `loadout_start_match_button_normal.png` and
  `loadout_start_match_button_pressed.png` as the geometry, material, and
  interaction references.
- Preserve the same fantasy-game craftsmanship, bevel structure, silhouette,
  ornament placement, and controlled highlights as the gold family.
- Do not use the red button family as a palette reference; this family must
  read as dark and neutral, not red.

## Output sizes

Generate one transparent normal background and one pressed background for
each distinct size below. Every PNG canvas is RGBA and rendered at 4x the
target dp dimensions.

| Family entry | Target display size | PNG canvas size |
|---|---:|---:|
| XS | 128 x 32 dp | 512 x 128 px |
| S | 176 x 44 dp | 704 x 176 px |
| M | 220 x 55 dp | 880 x 220 px |
| L | 280 x 70 dp | 1120 x 280 px |
| XL | 360 x 90 dp | 1440 x 360 px |
| XS short | 96 x 32 dp | 384 x 128 px |
| XS long | 160 x 32 dp | 640 x 128 px |

The XS normal size is 128 x 32 dp and is shared by the standard XS entry and
the XS length variants. Do not generate it twice. This results in exactly
14 distinct PNG files: seven footprints, each with normal and pressed states.

## Filenames and destination

Use `<family>_<size>[_<length>]_<state>.png`, where `<family>` is
`ui_button_dark`, `<state>` is `normal` or `pressed`, and `<length>` is used
only for the compact XS short and long variants.

- `ui_button_dark_xs_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xs_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_s_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_s_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_m_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_m_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_l_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_l_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xl_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xl_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xs_short_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xs_short_pressed.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xs_long_normal.png`
- `ui_button_dark_xs_long_pressed.png`

Save the 14 review assets under `assets_src/loadout/ui/`. Do not copy them to
Android resources until the user approves the preview.

## Shared visual design

- Keep the gold family's exact target proportions and silhouette for every
  matching size. Preserve its corner cuts, bevel widths, safe margins, and
  decorative side details.
- Use a rich charcoal or graphite face with near-black recessed shadows and
  restrained neutral highlights. The face must read as dark, not as a washed
  out gray.
- Retain the family's bronze/gold outer bevel and metallic trim so the dark
  buttons remain part of the same Urkaaaz button system.
- Keep the center text-safe area calm and unobstructed.
- These are background assets only. Android renders live labels separately.
  Do not include text, letters, numbers, icons, arrows, or labels in any PNG.
- Live labels use Cinzel SemiBold in warm ivory or pale gold for strong
  contrast against the dark face in both interaction states.
- Dark is for secondary, navigation, and utility actions. Keep primary
  continuation actions in the gold family and retry, restart, or destructive
  actions in the red family.
- Use transparent pixels outside the button silhouette; do not flatten a
  screen, panel, or other UI into a button.

## Interaction states

- **Normal:** visibly raised charcoal face, crisp upper bevel, and restrained
  highlights. It must read as enabled, not disabled.
- **Pressed:** preserve the exact outer geometry and ornament placement of
  its normal pair. Slightly deepen the face, reduce the raised bevel and
  highlights, and make the inner face feel gently pressed inward.
- Keep each normal/pressed pair pixel-aligned in silhouette and ornament
  placement. Pressed assets must remain clearly dark and enabled, with enough
  contrast for the live label.
- Do not add disabled, selected, loading, focus, or hover states.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, words, labels, logo, watermark, signature, opaque
background, full-screen UI, screenshot, phone frame, changed silhouette,
changed proportions, clipped corners, cropped bevel, asymmetrical ornaments,
ornaments in the text-safe area, excessive glow, bright gray or silver face,
blue face, red face, gold face, flat featureless black face, disabled state,
loading state, extra icons, extra buttons

## Review checklist

- Confirm exactly 14 files exist with the listed names and target pixel sizes.
- Confirm every PNG is RGBA with transparency outside the button silhouette.
- Confirm the five standard sizes exactly match the gold family's dimensions.
- Confirm XS short and long use the same 32 dp height and silhouette family;
  only their width and center plate change.
- Compare every normal/pressed pair as an overlay; geometry and ornament
  placement must align.
- Preview each size at its target dp dimensions and verify warm ivory/pale-gold
  live-label contrast in both states.
- Show all seven normal/pressed pairs individually for review before Android
  integration.
